  "worked_solution": "The osculating plane passes through the point $P$, which is at the tip of the vector $r(\\pi ).$ The vectors $T(\\pi )$ and $N(\\pi )$ are parallel to this plane. Therefore, a parametric equation for the plane can be written as\n\n$$\nR(s,u)=r(\\pi )+s\\,T(\\pi )+u\\,N(\\pi ),\\,s,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\pi ) & =\u27e8-3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\pi ,\\,4\\pi ,3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\pi \u27e9=\u27e83,4\\pi ,0\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, a parametric equation for the osculating plane at the point $(3,4\\pi ,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s,u) & =r(\\pi )+s\\,T(\\pi )+u\\,N(\\pi ) \\\\  & =\u27e83,4\\pi ,0\u27e9+s\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\u27e80,4,-3\u27e9+u\u27e8-1,0,0\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83-u,\\,4\\pi +\\frac{4s}{5},\\,-\\frac{3s}{5}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
